    resolution: "You plait the last handful and hold it high while the reapers cry \"The neck!\" three times, long and slow, and then \"We yen!\", and it rolls right across the valley. Then you run. However it goes at the dairy door, the neck is hung up in the farmhouse for next year, and the harvest supper is the best you've eaten. Then the practical half, for a harvest field. Farming kills more workers for its size than any other trade in Britain, so before anyone goes near a jammed machine: handbrake on, controls in neutral, engine off, key out, and wait for everything to stop turning. No child under thirteen rides on or drives a tractor or a combine; the field is not a playground. Keep high machinery well clear of overhead lines, and if a machine touches one, stay in the cab and ring 105, or if you must get out, jump clear without touching it and the ground at once. In the heat, tiredness, a headache, dizziness, cramps or a great thirst is heat exhaustion: into the shade, clothes loosened, water, skin sponged and fanned, and if they're no better in half an hour, or the skin is hot and dry, or they're confused, ring 999. And the kiss at the dairy door is Loveday's to give: kissing someone who hasn't agreed can be sexual assault, and the bucket is her answer if she says no.",
